-- title:
--   Places of K(t) for K algebraically closed: P¹(K)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field and let $v$ be a place of the rational function field $\mathrm{RatFunc}\,K$ over $K$, that is, a term of the project structure `Place K (RatFunc K)`: a valuation subring of $\mathrm{RatFunc}\,K$ which contains the image of $K$ under the structure map, is not the whole field, and is a principal ideal ring. The conclusion is a disjunction: either there is an element $a \in K$ with $v =$ `placeOfPoint K a`, the place attached to the irreducible polynomial $X - C(a)$ (namely `Place.ofHeightOneSpectrum` applied to the height-one prime of $K[X]$ generated by $X - C(a)$), or $v =$ `placeInfty K`, the place whose valuation subring is the valuation subring of `RatFunc.inftyValuation K`. Thus the places of $K(t)/K$ for $K$ algebraically closed are exhausted by the points $a \in K$ together with the point at infinity. The statement asserts only that this list is exhaustive; disjointness of the two cases and injectivity of $a \mapsto$ `placeOfPoint K a` are not part of it.
--
--   This is the classification of the places of a rational function field, specialised to an algebraically closed constant field, where the finite places correspond to the linear monic polynomials and hence to the points of $\mathbb{A}^1(K)$, so that the full set of places is identified with $\mathbb{P}^1(K) = K \cup \{\infty\}$. It serves as a basic tool in the function-field part of the development, used wherever an argument proceeds by cases over all places of $K(t)$, for instance in results on divisors, charts of annuli, and comparisons of places under constant field extension.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_RationalFunctionField_eq_placeOfPoint_or_eq_placeInfty.lean

